{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s","id":1030440,"title":"How to pick Shadow Name's for a consiliuns worth of npc's..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T22:19:45-08:00","id":1030440,"title":"How to pick Shadow Name's for a consiliuns worth of npc's..","content":"Hey All,<br /> <br /> I'm running into a creative block with picking shadow names for all the npc's for the chronicle I'm writing. Having decided I just can't have everyone named after a character from Arthurian mythology or the Mabinogion I rapidly feel like I'm scraping the bottom of barrel. I also realise at some point I'm gonna need to come up with a improve names mid game for that-third-arrow-mastitgos-from-the-right ect and there is definitely seems to be a law of diminishing returns when it comes to plumbing lists of various mythological figures and deities, abd most awakened would be really weary with those sorts of Shadow names because of the metaphysical wiether that thier narrative brings.<br /> <br /> What resources or other sources of inspiration do you use for Shadow Names?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:33:20-08:00","id":1030442,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, I go with mythology and religion; gods, saints, angels, demons, etc. There's tons of resources on that out there.<br /> <br /> That said, you really don't need to go with that. Many Mages will choose Shadow Names in purely descriptive terms; sometimes in English, sometimes in another language. Shadow Names with a cultural weight are a double-edged sword, since they draw you into their narrative, whereas a name like Golden Eyes or Convergence-of-Rivers (Goldie and River to their friends?) is much more personal; it may not have mythological weight, but you can give it such through your actions and deeds.<br /> <br /> If you've got multiple Mages from the same cabal, name them on a theme if you feel like it. Otherwise, just improvise at the time. If they're just a bit character, don't worry too much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:45:05-08:00","id":1030444,"title":"","content":"Break out the adjectival phrases and tack them on a regular pseudonym picked out of a baby-names book \u2014 Addison of the Iron Spade, Marilyn the Red, Two-Hit Luke, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Alternately, stick with less storied names. Themed cabals are good for this \u2014 a cabal built around the seasons or the noble gases or characters from the Wizard of Oz gives you at least a handful of things to call a wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:45:14-08:00","id":1030445,"title":"","content":"I usually get mine from myths and history. But don't limit yourself to 'proper' names. Rime. Nirvana. Sword.<br /> <br /> A few of mine are Ogun, Whaler, Oathkeeper, Chiron, the Morrigan, Great Old One, Carnacki, Vritra, Cobalus taken from Prometheus, Rakshasa, Yasunori Kat\u014d, Blome and Bullet. There's no Free Council or there would probably be more modern-themed ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:55:10-08:00","id":1030449,"title":"","content":"As another example, from my own game, a Thyrsus who goes by Morrigan Leighis (a butchered attempt on my part with Irish Gaelic; I believe it's pronounced &quot;Laysh&quot;). &quot;Morrigan the Healer&quot;, as approximately as I could make it, for a character whose specialties lie in shapeshifting, spirits, and healing.<br /> <br /> Edit: And from another game, Leopard, so named because his body is coated in tattoos from neck to ankles in spots. It has only just occurred to me that the character was formerly a member of a veeeery Left-Handed cabal (of whom he is the only survivor), who survived by reforming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T23:18:40-08:00","id":1030450,"title":"","content":"Drawing from popular culture can work too, particularly for Libertines, as long as it's not too obvious. Names of influential writers or musicians are one option; the Transhuman Engineers were founded by a mage who went by V.V., after Vernor Vinge, and I've been toying with the idea of creating a Libertine Mastigos who goes by Barker, after Clive Barker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T23:50:16-08:00","id":1030456,"title":"","content":"Start hitting <a href=\"https://www.theyfightcrime.org/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theyfightcrime.org/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T00:27:48-08:00","id":1030462,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a>, you now made my day with that generator! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We also had a rather <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/277637-good-shadow-names\">long topic on example mages from our games</a>, so it can be like 1000 Shadow Names made for particular characters ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:05:44-08:00","id":1030480,"title":"","content":"In the case of third-mastigos-from-the-right the Shadow Name doesn't actually have to mean anything, so don't over think it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:23:53-08:00","id":1030484,"title":"","content":"Maybe go over with first Path associated image that pops in to your head? Mastigos are about boundaries and fears so even Names like 'Bat' will have meaningful implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T06:25:33-08:00","id":1030543,"title":"","content":"And there should always be one guy whose shadow name is just &quot;Bob&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:15:03-08:00","id":1030563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030543#post1030543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there should always be one guy whose shadow name is just &quot;Bob&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And he likes to go one with human skull as his Dedicated Tool? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:20:24-08:00","id":1030565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030563#post1030563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And he likes to go one with human skull as his Dedicated Tool? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, he just drives psychologists insane via a variety of invasive tactics including stalking, impersonating an officer, emotional blackmail, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:54:41-08:00","id":1030669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030456#post1030456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Start hitting <a href=\"https://www.theyfightcrime.org/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theyfightcrime.org/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>They Fight Crime!</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's an oversexed moralistic grifter with no name. She's an orphaned antique-collecting single mother from beyond the grave They fight crime!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the third result I got, and had to share.<br /> <br /> that said </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.seventhsanctum.com/generate.php?Genname=superheronameorg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.seventhsanctum.com/graphics/7Slogo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.seventhsanctum.com/generate.php?Genname=superheronameorg\" target=\"_blank\"> Seventh Sanctum: the page of generators - random tools for art, gaming, writing, and imagination. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.seventhsanctum.com/generate.php?Genname=superheronameorg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.seventhsanctum.com/generate.php?Genname=superheronameorg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A site of generators to randomly produce concepts, characters, and descriptions for stories, role-playing games, and art, as well as have fun and alleviate creative blocks. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> is a resource you can use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:18:28-08:00","id":1030680,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend looking through Wikipedia categories:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Iconography\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Iconography\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Iconography - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Iconography\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Iconography </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Buddhist_ritual_implements\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Buddhist_ritual_implements\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Buddhist ritual implements - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Buddhist_ritual_implements\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Buddhist_ritual_implements </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_rocks\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_rocks\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Sacred rocks - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_rocks\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_rocks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Ritual_weapons\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Ritual_weapons\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Ritual weapons - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Ritual_weapons\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Ritual_weapons </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_trees\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_trees\" target=\"_blank\"> Category:Sacred trees - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_trees\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Sacred_trees </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_art_movements\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_art_movements</a><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Mythological_peoples\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catego...ogical_peoples</a><br /> <br /> You're bound to find something meaningful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:05:39-08:00","id":1030843,"title":"","content":"You can name people after anything. Some of my favorite 'shadow names' are from Neverwinter Nights 2, Sand and Bishop. They just took normal words and used those as their name. Bishop was an evil ranger and Sand was a wizard of some persuasion, but that completely doesn't matter. It's just cool to have some guy named Sand. <br /> <br /> If you want to make it more structured, divide your consilium into cabals and have their shadow names reflect their cabal theme. In 1E there was a cabal who took baseball as their theme, named something like &quot;The Sacred Game of Geometric Perfection.&quot; You could have consilium members named Mantle, Ruth, Ball and Bat. You're just thinking of terms associated with the over-arcing concept.<br /> <br /> A Free Council cabal based around some university's physics department: Tesla, Rutherford, de Broglie and Heisenberg<br /> <br /> A Mysterium cabal based around the concept of money: Krugerrand, Dollar, Guilder, and Florin<br /> <br /> An Adamantium Arrow cabal based around MMA: McGregor, Fedor, Crocop and Werdum<br /> <br /> A Silver Ladder cabal based around influence: Carnegie, Nash, Kahneman and Tverski<br /> <br /> A Guardian cabal based around secrecy: Connery, Brosnan, Moore and Craig. <br /> <br /> You just think of one thing initially, and then you form the whole cabal around that idea. It took me maybe 10 minutes to write this post, and I came up with 16 shadow names. You can spend a little more time and come up with more and better ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:23:32-08:00","id":1030852,"title":"","content":"I second the idea of picking a word and using it as a name. I rarely use mythology as a source for names, because I find it, 8 out of 10 times, incredibly pretentious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:32:33-08:00","id":1030853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030852#post1030852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rarely use mythology as a source for names, because I find it, 8 out of 10 times, incredibly pretentious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, that's a good excuse for a mage to have done it.<br /> <br /> But yes, keep in mind it if you're choosing to be named after a god, it's not just like that being your handle on a forum, it's what you would answer to and expect people to call you. Naming yourself after one would be a big statement about what you think of yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:41:28-08:00","id":1030856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030853#post1030853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, keep in mind it if you're choosing to be named after a god, it's not just like that being your handle on a forum,</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest that it is, unless you have invested in the shadow name perk. If you call yourself Persephone you're not going to spend 2/3rds of your playtime in Stygia, but if you invest in the 3 dot shadow name perk you just might end up spending most of your time enthralled to a drug dealer on the wrong side of the tracks who's made some sort of arrangement with your pimp.<br /> <br /> edit: which would then make a good scenario to RP your way out of. You're still going to be faced with the spectre of mythology hanging over your game, but it's going to be cool and interesting to play around in whatever it is you want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T01:21:40-08:00","id":1031495,"title":"","content":"You can mine history or Mother Nature for a plethora of Shadow Names:<br /> <br /> Ancient coins: Obol, Hyperpyron, Nomisma, Florin, Ducat<br /> Plants: Mandragora, Hycaninth, Dama de Noche, Hemlock<br /> Colors: Pthalo Green, Cadmium Red, Yellow Ochre, Bone Black<br /> 5 Stages of Grief (in Greek): Arnisi, Thymos, Diapragmatefsis (call me Dia for short), Katathlipsi (Kat), Apodochi<br /> 4 Chinese directions / constellations: Quinlong, Xuwanwu, Zhu Que, Bai Ho (Changeling uses this)<br /> Places carved out of cliffs: Ellora, Lalibela, Petra, Longmen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T14:50:28-08:00","id":1039614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1030440-how-to-pick-shadow-name-s-for-a-consiliuns-worth-of-npc-s?p=1030449#post1030449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another example, from my own game, a Thyrsus who goes by Morrigan Leighis (a butchered attempt on my part with Irish Gaelic; I believe it's pronounced &quot;Laysh&quot;). &quot;Morrigan the Healer&quot;, as approximately as I could make it, for a character whose specialties lie in shapeshifting, spirits, and healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops! Missed this.<br /> <br /> Morrigan the healer would be:<br /> M\u00f3rr\u00edoghan, An Liaigh (more old fashioned: M\u00f3rr\u00edoghan, An t-\u00cdc\u00ed)<br /> or<br /> M\u00f3rr\u00edoghan, An F\u00e1thlia (emphasises magical aspects of healing)<br /> <br /> Pronunciation: (italics and underline indicate actual English word)<br /> M\u00f3rr\u00edoghan = <u><i>More</i></u> - <i><u>Reagan</u></i> (like the president)<br /> An = un (i.e. <u>un</u>derstand)<br /> Liaigh = Lee - ag<br /> t-\u00cdc\u00ed = <u><i>tea</i></u> - <u><i>key</i></u><br /> F\u00e1thlia = Faw (rhymes with thaw) - Lee - a<br /> <br /> Yours means &quot;Morrigan of curing/healing&quot;, which is probably fine for your purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":".  Looking at the IPA for American English, I changed one, was using Hiberno-English before 01-28-2017, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:09:08-08:00","id":1039651,"title":"","content":"No force on Earth could ever make me say &quot;More Reagan&quot;. Not after what the last one did.<br /> <br /> Heh. I kid. This is great. Nice to have an actual Gaelic speaker chip in.<br /> <br /> As it stands, yeah, I think I'll go with what I've got; partly because it's so established now and partly because this version actually works a bit better. I appreciate the chipping in, though, and will probably bother you if I need names in future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:22:24-08:00","id":1039662,"title":"","content":"A thread where people ask for linguistic help on their Shadow Names sounds like an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}